:"10.1200/jco.23.01159","issn":["0732183X","15277755"],"issn_org":["0732183X"],"issue":"12","journal":"Journal of Clinical Oncology","pages":"1378-1390","publisher":"American Society of Clinical Oncology","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Oncology","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85189800901"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6bc405ed-a539-4f84-a193-4a8cf93c8445","sdu-3b3974f3-2bbf-432d-9107-ee4097b2c669"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Patient-Specific Measurable Residual Disease Markers Predict Outcome in Patients With Myelodysplastic Syndrome and Related Diseases After Hematopoietic Stem-Cell Transplantation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.08-735200","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Cell replacement therapies for Parkinson's disease (PD) based on transplantation of pluripotent stem cell-derived dopaminergic neurons are now entering clinical trials. Here, we present quality, safety, and efficacy data supporting the first-in-human STEM-PD phase I/IIa clinical trial along with the trial design. The STEM-PD product was manufactured under GMP and quality tested in vitro and in vivo to meet regulatory requirements. Importantly, no adverse effects were observed upon testing of the product in a 39-week rat GLP safety study for toxicity, tumorigenicity, and biodistribution, and a non-GLP efficacy study confirmed that the transplanted cells mediated full functional recovery in a pre-clinical rat model of PD. We further observed highly comparable efficacy results between two different GMP batches, verifying that the product can be serially manufactured. A fully in vivo-tested batch of STEM-PD is now being used in a clinical trial of 8 patients with moderate PD, initiated in 2022.","author_count":30,"contributors":["Kirkeby, Agnete","Nelander, Jenny","Hoban, Deirdre B.","Rogelius, Nina","Bjartmarz, Hjálmar","Storm, Petter","Fiorenzano, Alessandro","Adler, Andrew F.","Vale, Shelby","Mudannayake, Janitha","Zhang, Yu","Cardoso, Tiago","Mattsson, Bengt","Landau, Anne M.","Glud, Andreas N.","Sørensen, Jens C.","Lillethorup, Thea P.","Lowdell, Mark","Carvalho, Carla","Bain, Owen","van Vliet, Trinette","Lindvall, Olle","Björklund, Anders","Harry, Bronwen","Cutting, Emma","Widner, Håkan","Paul, Gesine","Barker, Roger A.","Parmar, Malin","Christiansen, Josefine Rågård"],"cuid":["S02-086.05-697968"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["Novo Nordisk Cell Therapy R&D"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Royal Free London NHS Foundation Trust","Skaane University Hospital","Skåne University Hospital","University of Cambridge"],"keyword":["ATMP","Animals","Cell Differentiation physiology","Clinical trial","Dopamine","Human embryonic stem cells","Humans","Minipig","Neurosurgery","Parkinson Disease therapy","Parkinson s","Rats","Regulatory","Stem Cell Transplantation methods","Stem cell therapy","Tissue Distribution","Transplantation","neurosurgical","pluripotent"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preclinical quality safety and efficacy of a human embryonic stem cell derived product for the treatment of parkinson s disease stem pd","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.stem.2023.08.014","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.05-697968","identifier":[{"id":"85174454209","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37802036","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-97e0d460-3e16-4b39-b285-bdbaaacf8d3b","ku-90227fae-2a87-4e8c-a0bb-8351a5f93a15"],"keyword":["ATMP","Animals","Cell Differentiation/physiology","Dopaminergic Neurons/physiology","Human Embryonic Stem Cells","Humans","Parkinson Disease/therapy","Parkinson's","Rats","Stem Cell Transplantation/methods","Tissue Distribution","clinical trial","dopamine","minipig","neurosurgery","neurosurgical","pluripotent","regulatory","stem cell therapy","transplantation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-30E8F36AC47A9248D2E2798550972119"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/371289699/1_s2.0_S1934590923003211_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https: