,"title":"Preclinical quality, safety, and efficacy of a human embryonic stem cell-derived product for the treatment of Parkinson's disease, STEM-PD","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.05-697968","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Cell replacement is a long-standing and realistic goal for the treatment of Parkinsonʼs disease (PD). Cells for transplantation can be obtained from fetal brain tissue or from stem cells. However, after transplantation, dopamine (DA) neurons are seen to be a minor component of grafts, and it has remained difficult to determine the identity of other cell types. Here, we report analysis by single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) combined with comprehensive histological analyses to characterize intracerebral grafts from human embryonic stem cells (hESCs) and fetal tissue after functional maturation in a pre-clinical rat PD model. We show that neurons and astrocytes are major components in both fetal and stem cell-derived grafts. Additionally, we identify a cell type closely resembling a class of recently identified perivascular-like cells in stem cell-derived grafts. Thus, this study uncovers previously unknown cellular diversity in a clinically relevant cell replacement PD model.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Tiklová, Katarína","Nolbrant, Sara","Fiorenzano, Alessandro","Björklund, Åsa K.","Sharma, Yogita","Heuer, Andreas","Gillberg, Linda","Hoban, Deirdre B.","Cardoso, Tiago","Adler, Andrew F.","Birtele, Marcella","Lundén-Miguel, Hilda","Volakakis, Nikolaos","Kirkeby, Agnete","Perlmann, Thomas","Parmar, Malin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-524414"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institutet","Ludwig Institute for Cancer Research","Lund University","Uppsala University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"single cell transcriptomics identifies stem cell derived graft composition in a model of parkinson s disease","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-16225-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-524414","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7229159","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32415072","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85084707734","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-db4b5aba-d6f9-4b30-8208-5f61bf405421"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-538DB65F60C44931DF0B7B1DDD6342DC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-16225-5","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/258441044/Single_cell_transcriptomics_identifies_stem_cell_derived_graft_composition_in_a_model_of_Parkinson_s_disease.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"ludwig institute for cancer research","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig Institute for Cancer Research","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"karolinska institutet","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institutet","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Developmenta