antation Using Individualized Minimal Residual Markers : The Prospective Nordic Study NMDSG14B","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-580539","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: This study aimed to identify sub-groups of workers with different trajectories of sick leave due to musculoskeletal pain over 1 year, and to investigate the extent to which the identified trajectories are associated with personal, occupational, lifestyle, and pain-related factors at baseline. METHODS: Data on 981 blue- and white-collar workers were analyzed in the DPHACTO cohort (2012-2014). The number of days on sick leave due to pain was reported using text messages at 4-week intervals across 1 year. Latent class growth analysis was used to distinguish sub-groups with different trajectories of sick leave. A web-based questionnaire at baseline was used to assess personal, occupational (physical and psychosocial), lifestyle, and pain-related factors. Multinomial regression models were constructed to determine associations between baseline factors and trajectories of sick leave (referencing no sick leave), with adjustment for potential confounders. RESULTS: Four distinct sub-groups were identified, with trajectories of sick leave due to pain ranging from no sick leave (prevalence 76%; average 0.5 days/year) to some days and increasing sick leave due to pain over 1 year (2%; 89 days/year). The increasing trajectory of sick leave was associated with higher perceived physical exertion, more time in manual work, less social community and influence at work, less leisure-time physical activity, smoking, and more severe symptoms (e.g., multisite pain, low back pain intensity, and pain interference). CONCLUSIONS: We identified four distinct trajectories of sick leave due to musculoskeletal pain. The sub-group with increasing sick leave due to pain was associated with several modifiable physical and psychosocial factors at work and outside work, which may have implications for prevention.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hallman, David M","Holtermann, Andreas","Björklund, Martin","Gupta, Nidhi","Rasmussen, Charlotte Diana Nørregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-782033"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centre for Musculoskeletal Research, Department of Occupational and Public Health Sciences, University of Gävle, Gävle, Sweden."],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"OT":["Department of Community Medicine and Rehabilitation, Umeå University, Umeå, Sweden."]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sick leave due to musculoskeletal pain determinants of distinct trajectories over 000000000001 year","src":["nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00420-019-01447-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-782033","identifier":[{"id":"85067077539","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31165308","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["nfa-e791a1e9-da2f-406f-b664-3238443050f2"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EE32C9CF64C1DDDE37ADC397A2CDAA61"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00420-019-01447-y","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"centre for musculoskeletal research department of occupational and public health sciences university of gävle gävle sweden","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Centre for Musculoskeletal Research, Department of Occupational and Public Health Sciences, University of Gävle, Gävle, Sweden.","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Musculoskeletal Disorders and Physical Workload"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Department of Community Medicine and Rehabilitation, Umeå University, Umeå, Sweden."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David M","key":"hallmanpau","last":"Hallman","name":"Hallman, David M","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"holtermannpau","last":"Holtermann","locid":"fd559bce-74b0-4973-a2d9-dd622af8b0c8","name":"Holtermann, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0003-4825-5697","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"björklundpau","last":"Björklund","name":"Björklund, Martin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nidhi","key":"guptapau","last":"Gupta","locid":"7a76cee7-5700-4ffd-b68e-2e9b69101673","name":"Gupta, Nidhi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte D Nørregaard","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"180d2a5d-fe8e-4956-b192-48aed7083301","name":"Rasmussen, Charlotte Diana Nørregaard","name_org":"Rasmussen, Charlotte D Nørregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-1769-717X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31165308"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00420-019-01447-y","issn":["03400131","14315777"],"issn_org":["03400131"],"issue":"8","journal":"International Archives of Occupational and Environmental Health","pages":"1099-1108","publisher":"Springer Verlag","status":"p","title":"International Archives of Occupational and Environmental Health","volume":"92"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067077539"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["nfa-e791a1e9-da2f-406f-b664-3238443050f2"],"src":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Sick leave due to musculoskeletal pain: determinants of distinct trajectories over 1 year","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-782033","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We study the problem of counting the isomorphic occurrences of a k-vertex pattern graph P as a subgraph in an n-vertex host graph G. Our specific interest is on algorithms for subgraph counting that are sensitive to the maximum degree Delta of the host graph. Assuming that the pattern graph P is connected and admits a vertex balancer of size b, we present an algorithm that counts the occurrences of P in G in O ((2 Delta-2)^{(k+b)/2} 2^{-b} n/(Delta) k^2 log n) time. We define a balancer as a vertex separator of P that can be represented as an intersection of two equal-size vertex subsets, the union of which is the vertex set of P, and both of which induce connected subgraphs of P. A corollary of our main result is that we can count the number of k-vertex paths in an n-vertex graph in O((2 Delta-2)^{floor[k/2]} n k^2 log n) time, which for all moderately dense graphs with Delta <= n^{1/3} improves on the recent breakthrough work of Curticapean, Dell, and Marx [STOC 2017], who show how to count the isomorphic occurrences of a q-edge pattern graph as a subgraph in an n-vertex host graph in time O(q^q n^{0.17q}) for all large enough q. Another recent result of Brand, Dell, and Husfeldt [STOC 2018] shows that k-vertex paths in a bounded-degree graph can be approximately counted in O(4^kn) time. Our result shows that the exact count can be recovered at least as fast for Delta<10. Our algorithm is based on the principle of inclusion and exclusion, and can be viewed as a sparsity-sensitive version of the \"counting in halves\"-approach explored by Björklund, Husfeldt, Kaski, and Koivisto [ESA 2009].","author_count":4,"contributors":["Björklund, Andreas","Husfeldt, Thore","Kaski, Petteri","Koivisto, Mikko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384439"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Sweden"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations","Helsinki Institute for Information Technology","Lund University","University of Helsinki"],"keyword":["Inclusion exclusion principle","Isomorphic occurrences","Maximum degree","Subgraph counting","Vertex balancer"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"counting connected subgraphs with maximum degree aware sieving","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/http://www.dagstuhl.de/dagpub/978-3-95977-094-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384439","identifier":[{"id":"85063676476","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d7509174-d74b-4167-8127-38dca1702ce8"],"keyword":["Inclusion-exclusion principle","Isomorphic occurrences","Maximum degree","Subgraph counting","Vertex balancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-6C2FAEF8DA6F7AC34868E3C83F33CC33"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/http://www.dagstuhl.de/dagpub/978-3-95977-094-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83629711/LIPIcs_ISAAC_2018_17.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fi","key":"university of helsinki","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Helsinki","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fi","key":"aalto university","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aalto University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"fi","key":"helsinki institute for information technology","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Helsinki Institute for Information Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"björklundpau","last":"Björklund","name":"Björklund, Andreas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thore","key":"husfeldtpau","last":"Husfeldt","locid":"472021c7-73cc-44ba-a4ef-70cd2bed8601","name":"Husfeldt, Thore","orcid":"0000-0001-9078-4512","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Petteri","key":"kaskipau","last":"Kaski","name":"Kaski, Petteri","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikko","key":"koivistopau","last":"Koivisto","name":"Koivisto, Mikko","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9783959770941"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","status":"p","title":"29th International Symposium on Algorithms and Computation, ISAAC 2018, December 16-19, 2018, Jiaoxi, Yilan, Taiwan.","volume":"123"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063676476"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d7509174-d74b-4167-8127-38dca1702ce8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Counting Connected Subgraphs with Maximum-Degree-Aware Sieving","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384439","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Given an undirected graph and two disjoint vertex pairs s1 , t1 and s2 , t2 , the Shortest two disjoint paths problem (S2DP) asks for the minimum total length of two vertex disjoint paths connecting s1 with t1, and s2 with t2, respectively. We show that for cubic planar graphs there are NC algorithms, uniform circuits of polynomial size and polylogarithmic depth, that compute the S2DP and moreover also output the number of such minimum length path pairs. Previously, to the best of our knowledge, no deterministic polynomial time algorithm was known for S2DP in cubic planar graphs with arbitrary placement of the terminals. In contrast, the randomized polynomial time algorithm by Björklund and Husfeldt, ICALP 2014, for general graphs is much slower, is serial in nature, and cannot count the solutions. Our results are built on an approach by Hirai and Namba, Algorithmica 2017, for a general- isation of S2DP, and fast algorithms for counting perfect matchings in planar graphs.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Björklund, Andreas","Husfeldt, Thore"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384639"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Cubic planar graphs","Deterministic polynomial time","NC algorithms","Perfect matchings in planar graphs","Shortest two disjoint paths"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"counting shortest two disjoint paths in cubic planar graphs with an nc algorithm","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ISAAC.2018.19","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384639","identifier":[{"id":"85063688304","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e511a721-6ecb-49b9-a940-c996ef0f8af4"],"keyword":["Cubic planar graphs","Deterministic polynomial time","NC algorithms","Perfect matchings in planar graphs","Shortest two disjoint paths"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-913B3150AD4426F4F5D374F8DA4B6972"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ISAAC.2018.19","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83629740/LIPIcs_ISAAC_2018_19.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"björklundpau","last":"Björklund","name":"Björklund, Andreas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thore","key":"husfeldtpau","last":"Husfeldt","locid":"472021c7-73cc-44ba-a4ef-70cd2bed8601","name":"Husfeldt, Thore","orcid":"0000-0001-9078-4512","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.isaac.2018.19","eisbn":["ISBN 9783959770941"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","status":"p","title":"29th International Symposium on Algorithms and Computation (ISAAC 2018)","volume":"123"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063688304"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e511a721-6ecb-49b9-a940-c996ef0f8af4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Counting Shortest Two Disjoint Paths in Cubic Planar Graphs with an NC Algorithm","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384639","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"We reduce the problem of detecting the existence of an object to the problem of computing the parity of the number of objects in question. In particular, when given any non-empty set system, we prove that randomly restricting elements of its ground set makes the size of the restricted set system an odd number with significant probability. When compared to previously known reductions of this type, ours excel in their simplicity: For graph problems, restricting elements of the ground set usually corresponds to simple deletion and contraction operations, which can be encoded efficiently in most problems. We find three applications of our reductions: 1. An exponential-time algorithm: We show how to decide Hamiltonicity in directed n-vertex graphs with running time 1.9999^n provided that the graph has at most 1.0385^n Hamiltonian cycles. We do so by reducing to the algorithm of Björklund and Husfeldt (FOCS 2013) that computes the parity of the number of Hamiltonian cycles in time 1.619^n. 2. A new result in the framework of Cygan et al. (CCC 2012) for analyzing the complexity of NP-hard problems under the Strong Exponential Time Hypothesis: If the parity of the number of Set Covers can be determined in time 1.9999^n, then Set Cover can be decided in the same time. 3. A structural result in parameterized complexity: We define the pa- rameterized complexity class ⊕W[1] and prove that it is at least as hard as W[1] under randomized fpt-reductions with bounded one- sided error; this is analogous to the classical result NP ⊆ RP⊕P by Toda (SICOMP 1991).","author_count":3,"contributors":["Björklund, Andreas","Dell, Holger","Husfeldt, Thore"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382621"],"event":{"acronym":"ICALP","end":"2015-07-10","place":"Kyoto, jp","start":"2015-07-06","title":"The 42nd International Colloquium on Automata, Languages, and Programming","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Saarland University"],"keyword":["Exponential Time Algorithms","Hamiltonicity","Parameterized complexity","Parity Computation","Set System Restrictions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the parity of set systems under random restrictions with applications to exponential time problems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81821968/pbdm.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382621","identifier":[{"id":"84950138716","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5b261d61-818a-4a29-81f5-d9466e9714de"],"keyword":["Exponential-Time Algorithms","Hamiltonicity","Parameterized Complexity","Parity Computation","Set System Restrictions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9E8C296B52BF54B332FAA71D74DA20EE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81821968/pbdm.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"saarland university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Saarland University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"björklundpau","last":"Björklund","name":"Björklund, Andreas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Holger","key":"dellpau","last":"Dell","name":"Dell, Holger","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Thore","key":"husfeldtpau","last":"Husfeldt","locid":"472021c7-73cc-44ba-a4ef-70cd2bed8601","name":"Husfeldt, Thore","orcid":"0000-0001-9078-4512","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-47672-7_19","eisbn":["9783662476727"],"isbn":["9783662476710"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"231-242","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 42nd International Colloquium on Automata, Languages, and Programming, ICALP 2015, (6-10 July 2015, Kyoto, Japan)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84950138716"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5b261d61-818a-4a29-81f5-d9466e9714de"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Parity of Set Systems under Random Restrictions with Applications to Exponential Time Problems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382621","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Human embryonic stem cell (hESC)-derived dopamine neurons are currently moving toward clinical use for Parkinson's disease (PD). However, the timing and extent at which stem cell-derived neurons functionally integrate into existing host neural circuitry after transplantation remain largely unknown. In this study, we use modified rabies virus to trace afferent and efferent connectivity of transplanted hESC-derived neurons in a rat model of PD and report that grafted human neurons integrate into the host neural circuitry in an unexpectedly rapid and extensive manner. The pattern of connectivity resembled that of local endogenous neurons, while ectopic connections were not detected. Revealing circuit integration of human dopamine neurons substantiates their potential use in clinical trials. Additionally, our data present rabies-based tracing as a valuable and widely applicable tool for analyzing graft connectivity that can easily be adapted to analyze connectivity of a variety of different neuronal sources and subtypes in different disease models.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Grealish, Shane","Heuer, Andreas","Cardoso, Tiago","Kirkeby, Agnete","Jönsson, Marie","Johansson, Jenny","Björklund, Anders","Jakobsson, Johan","Parmar, Malin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-459604"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"monosynaptic tracing using modified rabies virus reveals early and extensive circuit integration of human embryonic stem cell derived neurons","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.stemcr.2015.04.011","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-459604","identifier":[{"id":"84930928346","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26004633","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6ec37b6a-18f9-478b-9712-7ee5956c0eed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-42ACB8781E12EDC0D975E07B78776777"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.stemcr.2015.04.011","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, The Danish Stem Cell Center, Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Shane","key":"grealishpau","last":"Grealish","name":"Grealish, Shane","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"heuerpau","last":"Heuer","name":"Heuer, Andreas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tiago","key":"cardosopau","last":"Cardoso","name":"Cardoso, Tiago","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Agnete","key":"kirkebypau","last":"Kirkeby","locid":"3daffb1b-bd5c-49f2-9b6c-7da0b831735a","name":"Kirkeby, Agnete","orcid":"0000-0001-8203-6901","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marie","key":"jönssonpau","last":"Jönsson","name":"Jönsson, Marie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jenny","key":"johanssonpau","last":"Johansson","name":"Johansson, Jenny","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"björklundpau","last":"Björklund","name":"Björklund, Anders","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Johan","key":"jakobssonpau","last":"Jakobsson","name":"Jakobsson, Johan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Malin","key":"parmarpau","last":"Parmar","name":"Parmar, Malin","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26004633"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.stemcr.2015.04.011","issn":["22136711"],"issue":"6","journal":"Stem Cell Reports","pages":"975-983","status":"p","title":"Stem Cell Reports","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6ec37b6a-18f9-478b-9712-7ee5956c0eed"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Monosynaptic Tracing using Modified Rabies Virus Reveals Early and Extensive Circuit Integration of Human Embryonic Stem Cell-Derived Neurons","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-459604","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
